WEBVTT


00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:05.980
Knit it Now memember recently requested
instruction to make finished slashes in

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.360
the middle of a knitted piece.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:11.920
She wanted to convert a hand knitting
pattern that used this technique.

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:16.000
First, have a cast on rag
or knitted swatch ready.

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:21.280
These need to be large enough to fill the
number of needles in the slash they'll be

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:24.490
used to make the second half
of the slash easier to knit.

00:00:25.515 --> 00:00:29.564
I'm assuming you know how to put your
machine into hold position, so that any

00:00:29.564 --> 00:00:32.625
needles that are pulled all
the way out do not knit.

00:00:34.004 --> 00:00:36.075
I'll refer to the right set of stitches.

00:00:36.105 --> 00:00:40.394
The center set of stitches, which is the
opening and the left set of stitches is

00:00:40.394 --> 00:00:41.894
you see them on the needle bed.

00:00:42.795 --> 00:00:48.195
Cast on and knit the desired length to the
slash put the left and the center needles

00:00:48.195 --> 00:00:49.394
and to hold position.

00:00:50.385 --> 00:00:51.825
With the carriage on the right.

00:00:52.005 --> 00:00:55.965
Set your machine to hold and
knit across the right needles.

00:00:57.535 --> 00:01:02.305
You'll notice that the yarn is in position
to work on the center set of needles.

00:01:02.635 --> 00:01:06.295
You'll be binding these stitches
off using the method of your choice.

00:01:08.095 --> 00:01:11.635
This bind off creates the
opening for the slash.

00:01:12.945 --> 00:01:17.535
Once you're done with the bind off,
push those center needles to out of work

00:01:17.535 --> 00:01:18.195
position.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:24.000
Notice that your yarn is now in position
to work the left set of needles.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:29.759
But your carriage is on the left, so you
need to make a free pass to get it to the

00:01:29.759 --> 00:01:30.869
right hand side.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.979
Push any needles with
stitches into hold position.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:39.550
With the carriage still on
hold, make your free pass.

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:44.949
Then push the left set of needles into
working position and knit to the left

00:01:44.949 --> 00:01:46.179
across these needles.

00:01:46.995 --> 00:01:48.915
You'll have completed the first row.

00:01:49.665 --> 00:01:53.775
The right set of stitches were knit, the
center set were bound off, and the left

00:01:53.775 --> 00:01:56.055
stitches were knit all in one row.

00:01:56.475 --> 00:01:59.055
Your row counter should
only advance to one.

00:02:00.065 --> 00:02:03.965
The next row we'll fill in the
empty needles to complete the slash.

00:02:04.445 --> 00:02:09.005
First hang the cast on rag or the
swatch on the center set of needles.

00:02:09.275 --> 00:02:12.605
This will allow you to hang weights
and make the knitting easier.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.350
Manually knit one row of Ravel cord.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:35.090
In this image, notice the yellow Ravel
cord and the bound off slash behind the

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:36.560
purple cast on rag.

00:02:39.335 --> 00:02:42.185
Make sure your carriage
is still set to hold.

00:02:42.485 --> 00:02:47.975
Both the center set of needles and the
right needles are in hold knit across the

00:02:47.975 --> 00:02:48.965
left needles.

00:02:59.695 --> 00:03:04.045
You'll notice now that the yarn is in
position to work the center needles.

00:03:06.225 --> 00:03:10.815
Using the method of your choice
cast on those center 20 stitches.

00:03:11.715 --> 00:03:14.955
This will finish the opening of the slash.

00:03:16.245 --> 00:03:17.865
When you're done casting on.

00:03:17.895 --> 00:03:21.735
You'll notice that your yarn is now
in position to knit the right set of

00:03:21.735 --> 00:03:24.495
stitches, but the
carriage is on the right.

00:03:25.215 --> 00:03:30.225
So put all of the needles in hold for a
free pass and position the carriage on the

00:03:30.225 --> 00:03:30.825
left.

00:03:31.674 --> 00:03:36.804
Be sure the left and the center needles
are in hold and then knit the right set of

00:03:36.804 --> 00:03:37.375
stitches.

00:03:56.385 --> 00:03:59.145
Now set your carriage to
knit all the stitches.

00:03:59.205 --> 00:04:02.595
Remove the hold setting
and knit across the row.

00:04:03.105 --> 00:04:04.665
The slash is complete.

00:04:05.235 --> 00:04:07.485
You can continue knitting as desired

00:04:17.615 --> 00:04:21.575
When you remove the Ravel cord and the
cast on rag, you'll see your slash.

00:04:23.445 --> 00:04:29.445
the pattern she was using called for a
number of random slashes and the edges

00:04:29.445 --> 00:04:30.735
just simply rolled

00:04:35.355 --> 00:04:36.705
Thank you for watching.

00:04:37.515 --> 00:04:41.805
The Knit it Now learning library has
hundreds of techniques on a variety of

00:04:41.805 --> 00:04:44.205
subjects at all skill levels.

00:04:45.525 --> 00:04:47.385
Please consider a subscription.

00:04:48.405 --> 00:04:51.555
And let us help you be a
better machine knitter.

